# Never wipe API sources

Commit `d7d3fc8` (“Cursor rules”) emptied production API files and broke `/api/v1/my/*`.

## Forbidden unless the user explicitly asks

- Truncating a file to 0 bytes
- Deleting `app/Http/Controllers/**`, `routes/api/**`, or `config/*.php`
- “Cleaning” a controller by replacing it with an empty class/file
- Touching application PHP when the task is only about Cursor rules/docs

## Especially protected

- `app/Http/Controllers/Api/v1/MyApiController.php`
- `app/Http/Controllers/Api/v1/AppConfigController.php`
- `routes/api/v1/customer.php`
- `config/app_mobile.php`

Rules/docs work: edit `.cursor/rules/*` or `AGENTS.md` only.
